# Copy this file to .env (exactly that name — see below) and fill in real
# values for local development. Never commit the filled-in file — see
# ENVIRONMENT.md.
#
# LOADING: `npm run dev`/`npm start` load this file via Node's native
# --env-file-if-exists=.env flag (package.json). It must be named exactly
# `.env` in this directory — `.env.local` is NOT read by anything here
# (that convention is Next.js-specific; see web/.env.local instead).
#
# IMPORTANT — shell/OS environment variables always win over this file.
# If DATABASE_URL (or any other variable below) is already set in your
# terminal session or in Windows' persistent System/User Environment
# Variables (e.g. left over from running `supabase db push --db-url
# "%DATABASE_URL%"` in the same shell), that value is used INSTEAD of
# whatever is in this .env file, silently. If the backend appears to
# ignore a change you just made here, check for and clear a stale
# DATABASE_URL (or other) variable at the shell/OS level first — this is
# the single most common cause of "the value doesn't seem to update".
#
# Every variable here is validated by src/config/env.ts. Variables marked
# "not used yet" are placeholders for a later phase and are safe to leave
# blank until that phase's documentation says otherwise.

NODE_ENV=development
PORT=4000

# --- Database (Phase 5 schema implemented; live project required for
# authentication to actually resolve/provision users — see
# DATABASE_IMPLEMENTATION_REPORT.md and GOOGLE_OAUTH_SETUP.md) ---
# From your Supabase project: Project Settings > Database (DATABASE_URL)
# and Project Settings > API (SUPABASE_URL, SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY).
# DATABASE_URL is what src/lib/db.ts actually connects with.
#
# SUPABASE_URL IS REQUIRED for authentication to work at all —
# src/auth/verifySupabaseToken.ts verifies every session token against
# Supabase's real JWKS endpoint (${SUPABASE_URL}/auth/v1/.well-known/jwks.json,
# ES256). Leaving this blank makes EVERY authenticated request (including
# GET /api/v1/me and GET /api/v1/subjects, which the web Dashboard calls)
# fail with 500 auth_not_configured — the backend process itself still
# starts and /health still responds, only requests that need auth fail.
DATABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_URL=
# Only needed for Phase 7+ Storage / admin operations via the Supabase
# client library — not used for authentication. Highly privileged — never
# expose this to any client, never commit it, never log it
# (SECURITY_ARCHITECTURE.md §10).
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# --- SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET is retired ---
# src/auth/verifySupabaseToken.ts no longer uses a shared JWT secret to
# verify tokens (it migrated to SUPABASE_URL + JWKS above). This variable
# is kept optional in src/config/env.ts for backward compatibility only —
# setting or leaving it blank has no effect on authentication.
SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET=

# NOTE: there are no GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID/SECRET or SESSION_SIGNING_SECRET
# variables here (present in earlier phase scaffolding, now removed —
# DECISIONS.md D36/D37). Google OAuth is configured entirely inside the
# Supabase dashboard, and this backend does not mint its own session token
# — it verifies Supabase's token directly on every request. See
# AUTHENTICATION.md for the full reasoning.

# --- File storage (Phase 8) ---
# Supabase Storage bucket, read by src/config/env.ts. Used only when
# SUPABASE_URL and SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY are both set; otherwise the
# backend falls back to local-filesystem storage. Don't leave this blank:
# an empty value overrides the code default.
SUPABASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=educational-files
